# ── Dependencies / build output ───────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.expo/
dist/
dist-check/
bin/
data/
*.log
.DS_Store

# ── Generated native projects ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ★ THE LEADING SLASH IS LOAD-BEARING ★
# An unanchored `android/` also matches mobile/modules/kavach-t0/android/, which
# is the ENTIRE Tier-0 native plane. EAS uploads the git tree, so the unanchored
# rule silently ships an APK with no foreground service, no silent multi-SIM SMS
# and no Direct Boot — and because the JS side uses requireOptionalNativeModule,
# it degrades quietly instead of failing loudly. Anchor to the roots only.
/android/
/ios/
/mobile/android/
/mobile/ios/

# ── Gradle output INSIDE a local module ───────────────────────────────────────
# `mobile/modules/kavach-t0/android/` is SOURCE and must stay tracked (see above).
# Only its build/ output is excluded — matched by directory name, never by the
# `android/` segment, so the rule cannot creep back over the Kotlin. Kotlin's
# generated lambda dex names also exceed the Windows path limit, so leaving these
# untracked is a correctness issue for `git add`, not just hygiene.
**/android/build/
**/android/.cxx/
**/.gradle/
**/build/.transforms/

# built APKs — never commit binaries (RISK 11)
*.apk
